# Line-ending policy.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For shell
# scripts that is fatal: every line gains a carriage return, so `set -euo
# pipefail` becomes an option named "pipefail\r" and the script dies on line 10.
# It breaks under WSL bash, under any Linux or macOS shell, and on the lab
# machines - and it breaks for every teammate the moment they clone.
#
# These files must keep LF endings whatever the platform.

*.sh text eol=lf
*.tsv text eol=lf

# Python and Markdown are endings-agnostic, but keeping them consistent means a
# diff never shows a whole file as changed just because someone opened it in a
# different editor.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never translate these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
